The weirdest part of the game was when I got to the top of the Wizard's
tower (on the way down; I wasn't actually inside the tower) and the Wiz
himself popped out to greet me!  I didn't know he was capable of (or
interested in) leaving his tower until I actually came to steal the
Book.  So he stole the bell and candelabrum, and I had to abandon any
idea of 'porting back to the main dungeon for some more polypiling and
inventory re-adjustment.  Quite annoying.  Luckily he didn't bother me
too much after that; I only had to kill him ten times (three or so with
a wand o'death), and I got to avoid his tower altogether.  Baaelzebub
was much more of a problem, but I finally managed to be rid of him as
well.

I found/was granted TEN artifacts in this game: Magicbane, Fire Brand,
Cleaver, Sting, Trollsbane, Mjollnir, Vorpal Blade, Orcrist, Demonbane,
and Frost Brand.  Some I got from my god, some from my corpse, some
from my roommate's corpse, and some from monsters.  I ended up using
Mjollnir most of the time, switching occasionally to Magicbane once I
got the Book to avoid getting cursed (but after awhile I abandoned that
strategy, remembering that it cost my two amulets of life saving in my
last game.  By that time I didn't really care much what got cursed
anyway).

I did some things for the first time in this game: attempted to open
the castle gate with notes, since my god actually gave them to me this
time (I ended up just blowing up the drawbridge after all though,
because I don't think I was standing close enough for the notes to work
and I was worried about getting squished); and gave $ to priests for AC
reduction (now that I knew the exact formula).

I never got teleport control, despite encountering many tengus.  Ended
up having to blow a wish on a ring, since I had eaten a leprechaun
earlier and was annoyingly bouncing around.

Helm of telepathy was quite useful in Gehennom; I was never surprised
by any monsters, as I could see them through the walls.

Didn't use the quest item at all (two-handed staff wouldn't allow me to
use shield of reflection).  I eventually stashed it in a box so the Wiz
wouldn't steal it and leave it for some monster to use against me when
I killed him.

Four down (priestess, wizard, barbarian, healer), lots still to go...

